-- Sporta — the size rows the catalogue is missing.
--
-- GENERATED by scripts/make-missing-variants.mjs. Safe to re-run: every
-- statement is INSERT IGNORE, so a row that already exists is left alone
-- and nothing is overwritten. It does not touch orders, prices or stock
-- counts that already exist.
--
-- STOCK IS 0 ON EVERY NEW ROW. Nothing here knows what is on the shelf, and
-- a guess would be worse than a zero: at zero the shop simply says "out of
-- stock" and cannot oversell. Enter the real counts in /backends -> Stock,
-- which reads and writes exactly these rows.
--
-- Sizes: S, M, L, XL, 2XL, 3XL, 4XL, 5XL — from this shop's own size_charts table.

-- PART ONE — 27 products missing part of the run,
-- 174 rows. This half changes nothing a customer can see today: the
-- sizes already on sale keep their counts, and the missing ones appear as out
-- of stock instead of being absent. Safe to run on a live shop mid-day.
--
-- PART TWO — 0 products with no rows at all, 0 rows.
-- This half MAKES THOSE PRODUCTS UNBUYABLE until counts are entered, because
-- today they sell with no size recorded on the order or the picking list.
-- Read the note above part two before running it.

